To find the positive difference between $120\%$ of 30 and $130\%$ of 20, we can start by calculating each value separately.

First, we find $120\%$ of 30:
\begin{align*}
120\% \text{ of } 30 &= 1.2 \cdot 30 \\
&= 36
\end{align*}
Then, we find $130\%$ of 20:
\begin{align*}
130\% \text{ of } 20 &= 1.3 \cdot 20 \\
&= 26
\end{align*}
Now, we can find the positive difference between these two values:
\begin{align*}
36 - 26 &= 10
\end{align*}
Therefore, the positive difference between $120\%$ of 30 and $130\%$ of 20 is \boxed{10}.

